{
  /*
    Component tests, type-checked as web code rather than as Node code.

    They render a renderer component, so they need `lib: DOM` and a JSX factory — and they must not
    get those from `tsconfig.node.json`, because handing DOM types to every test in the project is
    how a main-process module ends up quietly using `document` and passing the check. Same reasoning
    as the `@vitest-environment happy-dom` docblock in the tests themselves: the DOM is opted into,
    per file, not made ambient.

    Vitest does not read this file (esbuild strips types without checking them), which is exactly why
    it has to exist: without it a component test can be committed with type errors that only a build
    would find.
  */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "include": [
    "tests/components/**/*",
    "src/renderer/src/**/*",
    "src/renderer/internal/**/*",
    // The overlay layer's surfaces, which grew a directory of their own after this file was written.
    "src/renderer/overlay/**/*",
    "src/renderer/shared/**/*",
    "src/shared/**/*",
    "src/preload/api.d.ts",
    "src/preload/internal-api.d.ts",
    /*
      Preload modules, one by one, because a test in here imports each of them.

      The element picker's page half is all document: where its host hangs, which element a
      capture-phase listener saw, how many things a selector matches and whether any of them is still
      drawn. None of that can be asserted in the `unit` project, which is `environment: node` — so its
      test lives beside the component tests, and this project is a `composite` one that refuses to
      pull a file in through an import it was not told about (TS6307).

      Named file by file rather than as `src/preload/**`, so this stays a list of what is *tested*
      here. `tsconfig.preload.json` remains the project that checks the preload as a whole, with the
      settings a preload actually builds under.
    */
    "src/preload/picker.ts",
    // The cosmetic preload, for the same reason: when its host sheet lands is a question about a document.
    "src/preload/cosmetic.ts"
  ],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    // `node` for Vitest's own globals, which arrive through `vitest/globals`.
    "types": ["node"],
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.components.tsbuildinfo",
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@shared/*": ["src/shared/*"],
      "@renderer/*": ["src/renderer/src/*"],
      "@renderer-shared/*": ["src/renderer/shared/*"],
      "@renderer-internal/*": ["src/renderer/internal/*"]
    }
  }
}
